# Call-site ledger of mss at b7f4d62c6c5dc68fd60d43600f0e91012c8bc2e0.
# Decide every `undecided` line; see macro-benchmark/README.md.
#
# mss has no trace: every edge comes from reading (mss.md). Analysed source:
# src/mss (root src), 19 modules. Python >= 3.9, CPython and PyPy, on the
# declared Unix family (GNU/Linux among it), macOS and Windows; every platform
# branch runs (README, "Judgements").
# Native calls go through ctypes: a call of a foreign function is
# ctypes.CDLL.__init__._FuncPtr.__call__ (Sublist3r precedent); an errcheck
# function or a C callback of the package that the foreign call runs is a
# callee of the package site that makes the foreign call (callback rule, B5).
default reject mss.linux.xcbgen.Keycode.__eq__, mss.linux.xcbgen.Timestamp.__eq__: no operand of this comparison or `in` test, and no key of this dict or set operation, is a Keycode or a Timestamp: the package never reads Setup.min_keycode/max_keycode, and it only passes timestamps on to XCB requests; the operands are str, bytes, int, float, tuple, list, dict, set, thread, IntEnum and Enum values, XID instances or Visualid instances
default reject mss.linux.xcbhelpers.XID.__eq__: no operand of this comparison or `in` test, and no key of this dict or set operation, is an XID instance (str, bytes, int, float, tuple, dict, set, thread, IntEnum and Enum values, or Visualid instances); the XID sites (linux/base.py 73:26, 294:49, 369:55) accept the candidate explicitly
default reject mss.linux.xcbgen.Visualid.__eq__: no operand of this comparison or `in` test, and no key of this dict or set operation, is a Visualid instance; the Visualid sites (linux/base.py 112:38, 458:71, linux/xshmgetimage.py 175:71) accept the candidate explicitly
default reject mss.linux.xcbhelpers.XID.__hash__, mss.linux.xcbgen.Keycode.__hash__, mss.linux.xcbgen.Timestamp.__hash__, mss.linux.xcbgen.Visualid.__hash__: no XID, Keycode, Timestamp or Visualid instance is ever hashed: none is a key of a dict or a member of a set (the keys and members are str, int, float, thread objects, IntEnum members and tuples), and the hash() calls hash ints
default reject mss.base._PlatformSpecific.__repr__, mss.darwin.CGPoint.__repr__, mss.darwin.CGRect.__repr__, mss.darwin.CGSize.__repr__, mss.screenshot.ScreenShot.__repr__: no value formatted, printed or converted to str at this site is one of these objects (the values are str, bytes, int, float, bool, None, dicts of such values, tuples of ints, exceptions or client values); the package never formats a _PlatformSpecific or a ScreenShot; CGRect.__repr__ formats its CGPoint and CGSize fields and accepts those candidates explicitly
default reject mss.linux.xcbhelpers.XProtoError.__str__, mss.linux.xlib.XError.__str__: no value formatted, printed or converted to str at this site is an XProtoError or an Xlib XError, and super().__str__() in an exception class reaches Exception.__str__; the str(arg) of _shm_report_issue (linux/xshmgetimage.py) and the print of the caught exception in mss.__main__ accept the candidates explicitly
default reject mss.base.MSS.__enter__, mss.base.MSS.__exit__: the context manager of this with statement is a threading lock, a contextlib.suppress object, a memoryview or a file object, not an MSS; the one with statement on an MSS (mss.__main__ 102:14) accepts the candidates explicitly

